<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Yes or No Picker | Random Two-Choice Decision Tool</title><meta name="description" content="Need a simple tie-breaker? Use this free Yes or No Picker for low-stakes everyday decisions, with an optional best-of-three mode."><meta name="robots" content="index,follow"><link rel="canonical" href="https://wheelnamepicker.com.au/yes-no-picker"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/value-pages.css"></head><body><div class="top"><div class="nav"><a class="brand" href="/">Wheel Name Picker</a><div class="links"><a href="/coin-toss">Coin Toss</a><a href="/random-number-picker">Number Picker</a><a href="/activity-picker">Activity Picker</a></div></div></div><header class="hero"><span class="badge">Two-choice tool</span><h1>Yes or No Picker</h1><p>A tiny decision tool for moments when both options are genuinely acceptable. Choose a single result or best of three, then use your own judgement about whether the answer actually fits.</p></header><main class="wrap"><div class="tool"><div class="grid"><div class="field"><label for="question">Optional question</label><input id="question" placeholder="Example: Should we watch a movie tonight?"></div><div class="field"><label for="mode">Mode</label><select id="mode"><option value="one">Single pick</option><option value="three">Best of three</option></select></div></div><div class="actions"><button id="pick">Choose Yes or No</button><button class="secondary" id="again">Choose again</button></div><div class="result big-choice" id="result">YES / NO</div><div class="result" id="detail">No result yet.</div></div><div class="article"><section><h2>What a random yes/no tool can and cannot do</h2><p>This picker is a tie-breaker, not an adviser. It can be useful when the consequences are small and you truly do not prefer one option over the other. It cannot weigh cost, safety, relationships, legal obligations, health concerns or long-term consequences.</p><p class="note">If the decision matters enough that a random answer could cause harm or regret, do not leave it to this tool.</p></section><section><h2>Good uses</h2><ul><li>Whether to play one more round of a casual game.</li><li>Whether to start with option A or option B when both are equally suitable.</li><li>Choosing who goes first after each person has agreed to the random rule.</li><li>Adding chance to a classroom or family activity.</li></ul></section><section><h2>Single pick versus best of three</h2><p>A single pick gives one independent result. Best of three makes three independent picks and reports whichever answer appears at least twice. Best of three does not make the result more informed; it simply changes the format and can make a playful decision feel more dramatic.</p></section><section><h2>Notice your reaction</h2><p>Sometimes the most useful part of a coin flip or yes/no picker is your immediate reaction. If the tool says “Yes” and you instantly wish it had said “No”, that tells you something about your preference. You are never required to follow the result.</p></section><section><h2>Related simple decision tools</h2><div class="cards"><a class="card" href="/coin-toss">Coin Toss<span>A familiar heads-or-tails tie-breaker.</span></a><a class="card" href="/dinner-picker">Dinner Picker<span>Choose from several meal ideas instead of two.</span></a><a class="card" href="/activity-picker">Activity Picker<span>Pick from a custom list of activities.</span></a></div></section></div></main><footer class="footer"><a href="/about">About</a><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a><a href="/terms">Terms</a><a href="/contact/">Contact</a><p>© 2026 Wheel Name Picker · Ascension Digital Group</p></footer><script>const $=id=>document.getElementById(id);function run(){const n=$('mode').value==='three'?3:1,picks=Array.from({length:n},()=>Math.random()<.5?'YES':'NO'),yes=picks.filter(x=>x==='YES').length,final=yes>n/2?'YES':'NO';$('result').textContent=final;$('detail').textContent=(($('question').value.trim()?$('question').value.trim()+' · ':'')+(n===1?'Single pick: '+final:'Best of three: '+picks.join(' · ')+' → '+final))} $('pick').onclick=run;$('again').onclick=run;</script></body></html>